{"diagnosis": "TRAP asserted with tohost FAIL 0xdead during 256-word NOP fetch instead of clean fetch progress with no trap. decoder_trigger at picorv32.v:1446 fires on mem_do_rinst || mem_done, so data-phase mem_done re-triggers the decoder on a stale word that decodes illegal. Removing the mem_done term restricts trigger to instruction fetch only, preventing the spurious illegal decode and trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1446,5 +1446,5 @@
-		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst || mem_done;
+		decoder_trigger <= mem_do_rinst;
 		decoder_trigger_q <= decoder_trigger;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger <= 0;
 		decoder_pseudo_trigger_q <= decoder_pseudo_trigger;
 		do_waitirq <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost 0x1 PASS, no TRAP: cpu trap asserted, fetch progress over 256 NOPs"}

